 hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/132992825.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[In a fascinating blend of music and animal companionship, a California singer-songwriter is working on a groundbreaking album alongside her rescue horse, Yupia. Using his nose and teeth, Yupia has mastered playing the guitar and harp, creating a partnership that has captivated millions online. The album promises a heartwarming fusion of Yupia's unique sounds and Khramov's vocal artistry, showcasing the profound trust and bond formed between humans and animals.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/los-angeles-singer-taught-her-rescue-horse-to-play-the-guitar-and-harp-and-now-they-are-releasing-an-album-together/articleshow/132992825.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/los-angeles-singer-taught-her-rescue-horse-to-play-the-guitar-and-harp-and-now-they-are-releasing-an-album-together/articleshow/132992825.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-08-06T14:25:43+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI World Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-132992825,imgsize-1966939.cms"/></item></channel></rss>